 "notes": "Cut k28 from ~230 brands to the three or four network operators of each major market (US, Canada, Brazil, UK, Germany, France, Italy, Spain, Netherlands, Switzerland, Nordics, Japan, India, China, Australia) from the Wikipedia operator lists, plus leading MVNOs and UK test winners (Which? Recommended Providers; Expert Reviews awards). Twelve largest operators in m, the rest by country in r. Dropped dead brands (Blyk, The People's Operator) and micro-MVNOs/small-country operators (e.g. Andorra Telecom, FL1, Foroya Tele, Manx Telecom, retailer MVNOs like Lidl Connect, edeka-smart). Travel eSIM: only renewing plans kept (Holafly monthly, Ubigi monthly/annual). Airalo and Saily left out: the retrieved review describes them as one-off/pay-as-you-go packs, which the kind excludes. No independent test winners outside the UK retrieved (Opensignal/CHOICE/Consumer Reports not fetched). Old kind sources kept."
